  "example": "For a function preceded by a doc comment, an attribute, and an attached citation comment, a Rust-item input starts at the earliest attached line and ends at the function's final line. Its `text` contains those complete raw source lines. Inserting lines before them changes the displayed range without changing the input. {cite}`requirements.ci.rust_item_inputs`",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The only test that references this example is `add_input_modes_capture_raw_sources_and_refresh_idempotently` in `tests/commands.rs` (around line 780). I found no other `{test}` reference to it. It covers the first half of the scenario but not the last sentence.\n\n**Covered:**\n- `src/main.rs` has a doc comment, `#[allow(dead_code)]`, an attached `// {impl}` citation comment, and then `fn main() { fn nested() {} }`.\n- The test adds a Rust-item input with `--rust-item src/main.rs:4`.\n- It asserts that the stored `text` is exactly the four complete raw lines: the doc comment, the attribute, the citation comment and the function line.\n- It asserts that `info` displays `src/main.rs:1–4`. The range therefore starts at the earliest attached line and ends at the function's last line.\n- It checks that re-adding the input is unchanged and idempotent.\n\n**Not covered:**\n- The example also says that inserting lines before the item changes the displayed range without changing the input. Nothing in the test edits `src/main.rs` to add lines before the item. Nothing re-validates the stored input afterwards, and nothing asserts that the displayed range moves while the input stays valid.\n- I searched `tests/` for insertion, shift or move scenarios and found none.\n- The other `requirements.ci.rust_item_inputs` tests in `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs` cover symlinks, external inputs and disallow rules. They are not tied to this example and use one-line items without a shifted range.\n\nNo FIXME acknowledges this gap. The shift-invariance outcome is therefore unverified by tests, so the example is not fully covered.",
